    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d119-a1">

                <pb facs="0319" n="299" sameAs="frus:frus1864p2/pg299"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-09-05"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 5, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> In reply to your note of the 19th ultimo,
                    respecting the proceedings of the Florida at Bermuda, I have the honor to inform
                    you that her Majesty’s government have received reports on the same subject from
                    her Majesty’s colonial and naval authorities, and that, after due consideration
                    of the same, they are of opinion that, although some disposition was manifested
                    by the commander of the Florida to evade the stringency of her Majesty’s
                    regulations, the most commendable strictness and diligence in enforcing those
                    regulations was observed on the part of the authorities, and that no substantial
                    deviation, either from the letter or from the spirit of those regulations, was
                    permitted to or did take place.</p>
                <p>I have farther the honor to inform you that her Majesty’s government consider
                    that the conduct of the lieutenant governor of Bermuda, on the occasion in
                    question, was perfectly proper.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
